<</Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/Alt (Figure 1, in the shape of HashiCorp's tutorial diagram: the GitHub repository feeds a pull request and main. The pull request goes to the agent with Turf on the runner for the plan phase: plan, providers, verdict, and a dotted loop back to the pull request carrying the comment and the review. A person merges. Main goes to the apply phase, a ring: plan, compare, approve that exact plan, apply, verify, and plan again until nothing is deferred. Converged, the fleet on AWS Lambda; then production, the same ring under a stricter policy.)
